# Aegis privacy/anti-forensics userland — always on.
mat2
secure-delete
bleachbit
keepassxc
# metadata-free screenshots / image tools
scrot
# password / secrets
pwgen
# optional VPN client for layering (WireGuard)
wireguard-tools

# --- encrypted containers (VeraCrypt-style, Debian-native) ---
# gnome-disks (udisks2) gives a GUI to unlock/mount LUKS, TrueCrypt and VeraCrypt
# volumes. cryptsetup (in core) opens VeraCrypt volumes with `--type tcrypt
# --veracrypt`. tcplay creates & opens TrueCrypt / VeraCrypt volumes INCLUDING
# hidden (deniable) ones from the CLI. Together these are the Debian-native
# foundation for the Aegis password vault — no external VeraCrypt binary.
# (zulucrypt was dropped from trixie, so it is not used.)
gnome-disk-utility
cryptsetup-bin
tcplay

# --- firewall manager (user-requested) ---
# gufw is the familiar GUI firewall manager. NOTE: ufw is installed but left
# DISABLED — aegis-firewall's fail-closed nftables ruleset stays the active
# firewall. Enabling ufw would flush/override it and can break the Tor
# anonymity guarantee (see the hardware-security guide).
gufw
ufw
